{"nodes": [{"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_12j_testing_the_retry_loop_and_the_idempotency_key_md", "label": "12j-testing-the-retry-loop-and-the-idempotency-key.md", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "page", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/12j-testing-the-retry-loop-and-the-idempotency-key.md", "source_location": "L1", "frontmatter": {"title": "A retry loop has two halves that need two entirely different kinds of test \u2014 its policy is a pure function you can exercise with a fake that throws on cue, and its trigger is a read/write dependency cycle that only two Serializable transactions can create, and testing one while believing you tested the other is how a loop ships that retries the wrong SQLSTATE forever", "sidebar_label": "12j \u00b7 Retry loop and idempotency", "sidebar_position": "66", "description": "Unit-testing the retry policy without a database, forcing a real 40001 with a gated pair of Serializable transactions, proving the loop&#x27;s body is re-executed and what that costs, the duplicate-POST race against an idempotency key, and where fake timers finally are the right tool."}}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_12j_testing_the_retry_loop_and_the_idempotency_key_half_one_the_policy_as_a_pure_unit_test", "label": "Half one \u2014 the policy, as a pure unit test", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-postgres/12j-testing-the-retry-loop-and-the-idempotency-key.md", "source_location": "L15"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_docs_nextjs_pages_16_building_a_crud_api_with_postgres_12j_testing_the_retry_loop_and_the_idempotency_key_the_re_execution_test_which_is_the_one_people_skip", "label": "The re-execution test, which is the one people skip", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/nextjs/pages/16-building-a-crud-api-with-post